# s5_park_input_chunk_ffn: two paid levers (park on host, read back one ciphertext at a time) on the
# two largest program-owned arrays after s3:
#
#   patch_park_input_copy.py   `enc_ecd_x_copy`, the LN1 residual, parked for the whole attention
#                              block. 768 x 21 MiB = 16,128 MiB, not read until after bootstrap1.
#   patch_chunk_ffn.py         the FFN output never exists as a whole array. 3,072 x 9 MiB =
#                              27,648 MiB, which is exactly s3's `used` growth at after_intermediate.
#
# impl_lever: patch_park_input_copy.py patch_chunk_ffn.py
# Two levers in one step (step id names both).
# pool_attacked: vram
# pool_skipped: host
# object_attacked: test.cu:70:main
# object_skipped: PhantomSecretKey::encrypt_zero_symmetric
# object_skipped: mod_switch_scale_to_next
# cost_class: paid
#
# cost       second category (bytes leave device memory and return); runtime measured below.
# host skip  as s3_boot_layer_release (90.0% anon:[heap]; largest named row 23.8 MB; off-path.md).
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# measured
#   peak_reserved_kb  110,985,216 -> 108,429,312   -2,555,904 kB    -2.30%
#   peak_alloc_kb     103,046,739 ->  91,806,355  -11,240,384 kB   -10.91%
#   wall                    3,340 ->       3,345 s                  +0.15%
#   host peak           2,109,700 ->   2,171,588 kB                 +2.93%
#   disk bank                   0 ->  45,902,467,072 B  (45.9 GB written and read back)
#   gate              md5 01469da3..., byte-identical to s3, s2 and s0
# -2.30% below the 2.94% variation; published on peak_alloc_kb (byte-identical over four runs and
# images, s3 moved it 4.87%; here 10.91%).
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# growth series
#   phase                    s3        s5      s5 growth
#   keys_created         40,576    40,576       +40,576
#   before_attention     94,368    67,552       +26,976   <- was +53,792 under s3: Halved
#   after_attention      94,368    69,984        +2,432
#   after_layernorm1     96,416    79,680        +9,696
#   after_bootstrap2     96,416    87,872        +8,192   <- refill
#   after_intermediate   99,968    87,872            +0   <- chunk_ffn: this event is gone
#   after_gelu          108,384    96,544        +8,672   <- refill
#   after_bootstrap3    108,384   105,888        +9,344   <- refill
#   after_bootstrap4    108,384   105,888            +0
# largest growth event halved; peak -2.30%: later phases (bootstrap2, gelu, bootstrap3) refilled
# ~8,000 to 9,000 MiB each. Enabling half of s6_stream_boot23 (together -24.2%); published separately
# to show the refill.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# prediction -16,128 MiB (residual) + up to -8,416 (FFN chunking), ~-22%; measured -2,496 MiB (freed
#            blocks re-taken; second instance after s3_input_copy_fused).
# gate       byte-identical for the fourth consecutive step: 45.9 GB of round trips = memory-for-time
#            trade.
